    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-j/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Substitute the two given points (π/2, −7) and (π, 1) into f(x) = A sec 2x + B. −7 = A sec π + B 1 = A sec 2π + B Since the secants are respectively −1 and 1, the points give −A + B = −7 [B1] and A + B = 1. [A1] Adding the equations gives 2B = −6, B = −3, and A = 1 −B . = 4 Thus A = 4, B = −3 . [M1] [A1] (b) Put u = x + 3π/2. [M1] The equation 4 sec 2u −3 = 5 [M1] gives cos 2u = 1/2. [A1] For 0 ≤u &lt; 2π, this gives u = π/6, 5π/6, 7π/6, 11π/6. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-j/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Subtracting 3π/2, the solutions are x = −4π/3, −2π/3, −π/3, π/3 . [M1] [A1] Source clarification. The shifted argument gives 4 sec(2x + 3π) −3 = 5, hence sec(2x + 3π) = 2 and cos(2x + 3π) = 1/2. Thus 2x + 3π = π/3 + 2nπ or 5π/3 + 2nπ. Subtracting gives 2x = −8π/3 + 2nπ or −4π/3 + 2nπ; division by two gives x = −4π/3 + nπ or −2π/3 + nπ. The boxed solutions use the stated domain on the input to f. The scan extends the secant formula periodically and instead restricts x itself to [0, 2π), obtaining π/3, 2π/3, 4π/3, 5π/3.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
